  {
    "id": "heapless-1",
    "summary": "Deque::clear, HistoryBuf::clear and IndexMap::clear run element destructors before resetting state, so a panicking Drop leaves the container claiming dropped elements.",
    "location": [
      "src/deque.rs:237",
      "src/history_buf.rs:318",
      "src/index_map.rs:963"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-2",
    "summary": "HistoryBuf::write drops the old element in place before replacing it, so a panicking Drop leaves a dropped element in the live buffer.",
    "location": [
      "src/history_buf.rs:376"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-3",
    "summary": "vec::IntoIter::drop sets the inner Vec's len to 0 only after dropping the remaining elements, so on a panic the inner Vec's Drop runs over every element again, including ones already yielded.",
    "location": [
      "src/vec/mod.rs:1527",
      "src/vec/mod.rs:1529"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-4",
    "summary": "Deque::make_contiguous on a full wrapped deque can set back to N instead of 0, so after a pop_front the next push_back writes past the buffer.",
    "location": [
      "src/deque.rs:489",
      "src/deque.rs:654"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-5",
    "summary": "IndexMap's Pos packs hash and index into a NonZeroU32 assuming {0xFFFF, 0xFFFF} never occurs, so the 65536th entry of a full map with that hash calls new_unchecked(0).",
    "location": [
      "src/index_map.rs:103",
      "src/index_map.rs:104"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-6",
    "summary": "IndexMap::truncate clears index slots of removed entries without repairing probe chains, so keys still in the map cannot be found.",
    "location": [
      "src/index_map.rs:1269",
      "src/index_map.rs:1274"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-7",
    "summary": "pool::UnionNode has no repr(C), while Box and Arc pools cast a node pointer directly to the data pointer, relying on an offset of 0 the language does not guarantee.",
    "location": [
      "src/pool/treiber.rs:47",
      "src/pool/boxed.rs:331"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-8",
    "summary": "IndexMap::retain rebuilds its index only after Vec::retain_mut returns, so a panicking predicate leaves index slots pointing past the shrunken entries, and find reads them unchecked.",
    "location": [
      "src/index_map.rs:308",
      "src/index_map.rs:188"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-9",
    "summary": "Vec::retain_mut's BackshiftOnDrop takes a shared and then a mutable borrow of the Vec to get its two pointers, invalidating the first pointer before ptr::copy reads through it.",
    "location": [
      "src/vec/mod.rs:1168",
      "src/vec/mod.rs:1181"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-10",
    "summary": "BoxBlock::new and ArcBlock::new initialise only the union's data field as uninit, then manage() and the Treiber stack form a reference to the uninitialised next atomic.",
    "location": [
      "src/pool/boxed.rs:358",
      "src/pool/arc.rs:387",
      "src/pool/treiber.rs:56"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "heapless-11",
    "summary": "IndexMap accepts any power-of-two N although Pos holds a 16-bit index, so maps above 65536 entries overflow in Pos::new, lose keys, and can hang in remove.",
